# --- Required, previously absent (the app cannot start without these) --------
TENANT_ID=
TIME_SERIES_DB_HOST=localhost
TIME_SERIES_DB_REST_PORT=6041
TIME_SERIES_DB_USER=root
TIME_SERIES_DB_NAME=surveillance_fog
# TIME_SERIES_DB_PASSWORD is injected by docker-entrypoint.sh from
# TIME_SERIES_DB_PASSWORD_FILE. Set it here ONLY when running outside the container.

# --- Camera discovery: network scanner --------------------------------------
NMAP_EXECUTABLE=/usr/bin/nmap
# Guard against sweeping an unexpectedly large network. deriveNetwork() THROWS
# when a NIC's subnet has more usable hosts than this, which aborts that scan.
# 256 only covers a /24. A /23 needs 512, a /22 needs 1024. Set it to match the
# camera network or discovery returns nothing.
SCANNER_MAX_HOSTS=1024
SCANNER_PROCESS_TIMEOUT_MS=120000
SCANNER_MAX_OUTPUT_BYTES=10485760
# Read-only lease file; the channel is skipped with a warning if absent.
DNSMASQ_LEASE_FILE=/var/lib/misc/dnsmasq.leases

# --- Camera discovery: ONVIF ------------------------------------------------
ONVIF_REQUEST_TIMEOUT_MS=5000
ONVIF_CANDIDATE_PORTS=80,8000,8899,2020
ONVIF_DISCOVERY_TTL_MINUTES=60
# Ordered candidate list, tried per camera until one authenticates; first success
# wins and stops the loop. Compact JSON on ONE line, no spaces, no outer quotes.
#
# These are PUBLISHED vendor defaults, not secrets — safe to commit. Per-camera
# passwords set during Phase 3 commissioning are NOT, and must never land here.
#
# Sourced from a brand reference sheet, deduplicated: 20 brands collapse to 6
# distinct pairs because most share credentials. Ordered by how many brands each
# covers, Iranian brands first (they dominate the local market and use .1.21/.1.108
# defaults). REORDER to match your actual fleet — every camera pays one failed
# login for each entry ahead of its match.
#
#   1. admin/admin123 - Nazer, Clarent, Optina, Albatron   (all default 192.168.1.21)
#   2. admin/123456   - Uniview, KDT, B-Tech, SVision
#   3. admin/admin    - Avigilon, Pelco, Exsom, Hares
#   4. admin/111111   - Briton
#   5. service/service- Bosch
#   6. admin/(empty)  - Sony
#
# NO DEFAULT PASSWORD — these ship un-activated and CANNOT be discovered in
# Phase 1 no matter what is listed here. They will always report AUTH_FAILED and
# will absorb one failed attempt per entry above. They need the Phase 2 vendor
# adapters (SADP/ISAPI activation) to be reachable at all:
#   Hikvision (192.168.1.64), Dahua (192.168.1.108), Hilook (192.168.1.64),
#   Tiandy (192.168.1.2), Axis (root, 192.168.0.90)
# If your fleet is mostly these brands, keep this list SHORT — a long list buys
# nothing for them and only risks tripping vendor lockout thresholds on repeat scans.
#
# WARNING - this file is TRACKED IN GIT. Published defaults are fine; real
#   commissioned passwords are not. Those belong in a docker secret.
# WARNING - a '#' in a password BREAKS this line: dotenv truncates the value at
#   the '#', JSON.parse then throws, and AppConfig() fails on every access, so the
#   app will not start. Verified. ('$' and spaces are safe.) A camera whose
#   password contains '#' must go through a secret file, not this variable.
ONVIF_DEFAULT_CREDENTIALS=[{"username":"admin","password":"admin123"},{"username":"admin","password":"123456"},{"username":"admin","password":"admin"},{"username":"admin","password":"111111"},{"username":"service","password":"service"},{"username":"admin","password":""}]
